  "facts": [
    "Opened in 2001, the Folgefonna Tunnel stretches 11,150 meters, making it Norway's fourth longest road tunnel and cutting travel time between Eitrheim and Odda from four hours to a mere ten minutes.",
    "Beneath the massive Folgefonna glacier and National Park, the tunnel showcases advanced engineering that allows motorists to traverse a 36,580‑foot stretch of ice‑covered terrain without a single bridge.",
    "Since its inauguration, the tunnel has become a critical link in County Road 49, enabling a shorter, snow‑resilient route from Odda to Bergen when combined with the nearby Jondal Tunnel and a ferry."
